{
    "article_summary": "The article describes a rhodium-catalyzed direct hydrocarboxylation of styrenes using CO2 and H2 as the terminal reductant. This 100% atom-economical reaction is facilitated by visible light irradiation and proceeds under base-free, mild conditions (room temperature, 1 atm). The use of a cationic rhodium complex with Buchwald-type ligands (DavePhos) was found to be critical for achieving high selectivity for hydrocarboxylation over the competing hydrogenation pathway.",
